so with the impending release of God of  War three remastered on the ps4 we  thought we'd take a look at all three  mainline god of war games and compare  their openings all three are epic in  some way or another we thought we'd take  a look and see which one we think is  most epic first up God of War one its  memorable in its own way you fight the  Hydra as you move through the various  stages on boat and beyond not only does  the Hydra fight use god of war signature  QuickTime events but you also get the  chance to use traversal to your benefits  each time you face the Hydra the game is  a lot of fun very bombastic very big in  general it's the bits in between that  bring the opening down just a little in  some cases that means walking on narrow  beams in another case this means pushing  a crate around so that you can get to  higher ground  all well archers Pelt you with arrows  it's telling that by the time God of War  three comes around there is no more  walking around on narrow beams and even  in the case of God of War 2 the puzzles  during the opening sequence are a lot  more interesting than that stupid crate  pushing 1 all-in-all God of War Ones  opening is excellent and of course epic  however it is one upped by the two that  were to come later God of War two one  ups the original in almost every way  this is a fight against the great  Colossus of Rhodes and it is also of the  three openings for the main line games  the longest all in all this fight  remains very focused the Colossus of  Rhodes attacks you as you move from one  part of the level to the next and it  concludes with you actually entering the  Colossus of Rhodes and scaling his  innards so that you can finally bring  him down  the platforming sequence that closes  this opening may not be as epic as  climbing Gaia in God of War 3 but it's  certainly an interesting ending and  brings a lot more variety than just the  hacking and slashing and the QuickTime  events that came before if you were to  say that God of War two's opening was  the best of the three I don't know that  I would argue greatly with you on the  face of it God of War threes opening is  the opening to end all openings in this  case you're facing Poseidon multiple  times as you climb Gaia there are many  many moving parts to this level and  what's most interesting about it is that  Gaia keeps changing positions as you  fight Poseidon there are lots of games  in which you do battle on moving parts  and pieces but there's nothing quite as  stupendous as this God of War three  opening in which you go from climbing  Gaia to doing battle two QuickTime  events with Poseidon and so on and so  forth if there's a downside it's that  it's actually over fairly quickly at  least when you compare it to God of War  two's Colossus of Rhodes opening the  other downside might be that God of War  three opens so strongly that there isn't  a whole lot left to come that can really  stand up to that level of excellence in  their contexts I would probably argue  that God of War two's opening is  actually the stronger one however on its  own God of War three's introduction is  so incredible that it still stands as  one of the series high points when it  comes to God of War which opening do you  like the best  leave your vote in the comments below  you
 

